# Ignore EVERY .env variant, then re-allow the committed templates. The old list was `.env` +
# `.env.local` only, which did not match `.env.cloud` / `.env.production` / `.env.cloud.local` —
# and README.md + docs/LOCAL-CLOUD-TESTING.md walk the reader through filling one of those in
# with SESSION_SECRET, ENCRYPTION_KEY and the OAuth client secret. One `git add -A` away from
# publishing them in a public repository.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.cloud.example

